  "system": {
    "identifier": "lyonesse-wyrd-sorcery-wyrd-time-wyrd-time",
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>At the start of your turn, you can choose to slow the flow of time for everyone but yourself. Wyrd time lasts a number of rounds equal to your Charisma modifier and can be extended by the use of 1 Sorcery Point for 1 additional round while it remains. While Wyrd Time is in effect you gain the following:</p><ul><li>Your Speed is doubled.</li><li>Attacks against you are made with Disadvantage.</li><li>You have Advantage on saving throws.</li><li>Your movement doesn’t provoke Opportunity Attacks.</li><li>On your turn, you can take one of the following actions as a Bonus Action: Help, Hide, or Utilize. Wyrd Time ends if:</li><li>One of the actions you use during this period, or any effects that you create during it, affects a creature other than you or an object being worn or carried by someone other than you. You can also end it with a Bonus action. The Help action does not count for the purposes of ending Wyrd Time.</li><li>You gain one of the following conditions: Grappled, Incapacitated, Prone, Paralyzed, Petrified, Restrained, Stunned, Unconscious. Once you use this feature, you can’t use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you spend 5 Sorcery Points.</li></ul>"
    },
    "type": {
      "value": "class"
    },
    "requirements": "Wyrd Sorcery 6",
